__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
backend/storage/
backend/.env
.env
.env.local
# `.env` alone does NOT cover the `.env.<something>` variants — a
# `.env.local` holding live Supabase keys was sitting untracked and
# committable in this working tree.  `.env.example` stays tracked below.
.env.*
!.env.example
# Supabase CLI machine state: a linked project ref, pooler URL and local
# certificate. Migrations and config.toml are deliberately NOT ignored — those
# are source, and whether to track them is the repo owner's call.
supabase/.temp/
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Customer documents and a stray second git database, both of which were
# TRACKED and pushed. `.git1/` is a complete earlier repository of this same
# project — 378 files, its own object store and reflog — committed inside this
# one, where no `git log`, review or secret scanner would ever look at it.
# `ALL7_split/` is seven real commercial invoices.
#
# Both have since been purged from every commit on every branch (git
# filter-repo, force-pushed 2026-08-09), so these two lines are no longer a
# fig leaf over tracked files — they are what stops either from coming back.
# Keep them.
#
# What the rewrite could NOT reach: GitHub's `refs/pull/*` refs still point at
# the pre-rewrite commits, so `refs/pull/20/head` still resolves to a tree
# holding all 385 files. Those refs are read-only to clients; clearing them
# needs a GitHub Support request for object GC, or recreating the repository.
.git1/
ALL7_split/

# Local design tooling — the ui-ux-pro-max skill and its upstream clone.
# Everyone installs their own copy; .claude/launch.json stays tracked.
.claude/skills/
.claude/ui-ux-pro-max-repo/
.claude/worktrees/

# Your negotiated vendor rates (backend/vendor_prices.example.json is the
# template). Kept out of git: what a deployment is charged is its own business,
# and a committed rate table is one more thing to drift from the invoice.
backend/vendor_prices.json
